    "keeps the calibration from being circular.",
    "",
    "'relation' follows the decision matrix on issue #75:",
    "  identical   - same assessment, same wording",
    "  paraphrase  - same assessment, reworded, overlapping vocabulary",
    "  semantic    - same assessment, reworded with DISJOINT vocabulary",
    "  competency  - same concept, different competency tested (permit)",
    "  concept     - same topic, different concept (permit)",
    "  unrelated   - different topic (permit)",
    "",
    "duplicate=true means the gate is supposed to catch it.",
    "'semantic' pairs are the ones only a real embedding model can catch; a",
    "lexical scorer sees almost no overlap. They are in the set deliberately."
